{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1505","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1505","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1505\",\"parent_revision\":\"b893a535b34035086f8493ffdc1d8d96d622691cf76bfc86681bf747c042e80a\",\"root_revision\":\"b893a535b34035086f8493ffdc1d8d96d622691cf76bfc86681bf747c042e80a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nTwo FastMCP capabilities are absent from sam_schema/server.py: (1) Resource templates \u2014 plans and tasks map naturally to MCP resource URIs (`plan://{plan_id}`, `task://{plan_id}/{task_id}`). Currently clients must use a tool call (counting against tool-use limits) to read plan metadata. (2) Tool tags \u2014 all 8 tools are undifferentiated. Read-only tools (`sam_read`, `sam_status`, `sam_ready`, `sam_list`) carry no `tags={\\\"read\\\"}` and mutating tools (`sam_create`, `sam_update`, `sam_state`, `sam_claim`) carry no `tags={\\\"write\\\"}`. Tag-based filtering on composed servers requires tags to be declared at registration time.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**VERIFIED** \u2014 Both capabilities are absent. Evidence:\\n\\n- No `@mcp.resource` decorator anywhere in `server.py` (622 lines).\\n- All 8 `@mcp.tool` decorators use bare `@mcp.tool` with no parameters \u2014 no `tags=` argument on any of them (lines 111, 160, 186, 236, 301, 423, 510, 581).\\n- FastMCP resource template registration via `@mcp.resource(\\\"plan://{plan_id}\\\")` is a standard FastMCP pattern not currently used.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nType: **feature** (two independent missing capabilities; can be split or delivered together)\\n\\nRoot-Cause Analysis: Initial implementation focused on tool-based access only. Resource templates and tool tags are FastMCP enhancements not required for functional correctness but valuable for client ergonomics and server composition.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 add resource handlers after line 103 (after `mcp` declaration); update all 8 `@mcp.tool` decorators with tags\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` \u2014 add tests for resource template resolution (new test group)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Resource templates (higher impact)**:\\n- Without resource URIs, every plan/task read consumes a tool call slot (relevant for clients with per-session tool-call budgets).\\n- Clients that understand MCP resource semantics (read-only, cacheable) cannot treat plan/task reads as resources.\\n- Severity: low today (tools work fine), medium as MCP client ecosystem matures.\\n\\n**Tool tags (lower impact)**:\\n- Composed servers that route or filter tools by read/write cannot differentiate SAM tools.\\n- `sam_read` and `sam_status` are safe to expose in read-only contexts; without `tags={\\\"read\\\"}`, they cannot be filtered out from write-capable contexts.\\n- Severity: low (no current consumer uses tag-based filtering for this server).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #1504 (lifespan refactor) \u2014 if lifespan is adopted, resource handlers should also retrieve the backend from `ctx.lifespan_context[\\\"backend\\\"]` rather than `get_task_config()`. Deliver after or concurrently with #1504.\\n- #1503 (ctx:Context injection) \u2014 resource handlers can also accept `ctx: Context` for logging. Coordinate if delivered together.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Resource templates:**\\n- [ ] `@mcp.resource(\\\"plan://{plan_id}\\\")` registered, returning the same dict as `sam_read(plan=plan_id)` (no task)\\n- [ ] `@mcp.resource(\\\"task://{plan_id}/{task_id}\\\")` registered, returning the same dict as `sam_read(plan=plan_id, task=task_id)`\\n- [ ] Both resource handlers respect the default `plan_dir` sentinel (use the configured backend, not a hardcoded path)\\n- [ ] Resource handlers raise `ResourceError` (or let `PlanNotFoundError` / `TaskNotFoundError` propagate) on missing plan/task\\n\\n**Tool tags:**\\n- [ ] `sam_read`, `sam_status`, `sam_ready`, `sam_list` decorated with `@mcp.tool(tags={\\\"read\\\"})`\\n- [ ] `sam_create`, `sam_update`, `sam_state`, `sam_claim` decorated with `@mcp.tool(tags={\\\"write\\\"})`\\n- [ ] Existing tests in `test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` pass after decorator changes (tag addition is additive, no behavior change)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEstimate: **S**\\nReasoning: Tool tag additions are trivial (8 decorator changes). Resource templates require two new handlers with the same backend call pattern as existing tools \u2014 straightforward but need tests. Total: half-day.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nVerify both gaps:\\n\\n```bash\\n# No resource templates\\ngrep -n \\\"@mcp.resource\\\" plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py\\n# No tool tags\\ngrep -n \\\"tags=\\\" plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py\\n```\\n\\nBoth should return no output.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want **SAM MCP server to expose resource templates and tool tags** so that **plan/task data is directly addressable as MCP resources and read/write tools can be filtered at the server-composition layer**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: FastMCP review of P912 \u2014 .tmp/scratch/reports/fastmcp-review-P912.md\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ff15640cef4fb7dcb4dbeaa43f78782a56d81c9ccdc23fd385fc220cf157fa1b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSdr20Q\"}"}